# reduce_scatter_samerack.cm
#
# Reduce-Scatter over a 4-member group placed WITHIN one pod: hosts 0,1 share
# ToR0 and hosts 2,3 share ToR1 (K=4 fat tree). The aggregation apex is an
# aggregation switch in pod 0. block i -> host i, so the apex's descending
# unicasts for blocks 0 and 1 BOTH arrive at ToR0 and must resolve to the
# correct per-host sink (host-route keyed by (addr, op_flow_id)). This
# exercises multi-sink delivery when group members share a ToR.
#
# Vector 16384 = 4 blocks of 4096; each member ends with its own 4096 slice.
Nodes 16
Grp 0 1 2 3
Connections 1
0->0 id 1 start_reduce_scatter 0 size 16384
